AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_6000441> "IL-6 is a pleiotropic cytokine with functions such as production of acute phase proteins in the liver, haematopoiesis, osteoclast activation, proliferation and differentiation of B lymphocytes and also the induction of fever in the brain. IL-6 behaves both as a cytokine and myokine in the immune system, affecting many auto-immune diseases. IL-6 is well-known for its effects in diabetes, atherosclerosis, prostate cancer, encephalitis and also rheumatoid arthritis, acting as a pro-inflammatory cytokine reinforcing the inflammatory states.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_6000441> "Abnormal circulating interleukin 6 concentration")
SubClassOf(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_6000441> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0011117>)

